  "id": "DrugBank_DB01188 - MONDO_5915",
  "verbalization": "Ciclopirox, an antifungal agent, is linked to Pityriasis Versicolor through a chain of indications and off-label use. The evidence suggests that Ciclopirox is used off-label for conditions such as Tinea Pedis and Tinea Infection, both of which are fungal infections that can lead to Pityriasis Versicolor. This off-label use implies a potential therapeutic role in treating a condition that shares similar pathophysiological features with Pityriasis Versicolor. The connection is further supported by the indication of Ciclopirox for Cutaneous Candidiasis, another fungal infection, and its use of Econazole, an antifungal agent, to treat Pityriasis Versicolor. The overlapping mechanisms of antifungal action and the shared clinical presentation of fungal infections suggest a possible mechanism of action that could explain the relationship between Ciclopirox and Pityriasis Versicolor. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, highlighting a potential role of Ciclopirox in the treatment of fungal infections, including Pityriasis Versicolor, through its antifungal properties and off-label use.",
